<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">7 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 7 November, from 680 to 1940.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/680">680 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,346 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Third Council of Constantinople opens in the imperial palace</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Only 37 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> and several presbyters met in the Trullus, a domed hall of the imperial palace, to open the Third Council of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. By its close in 681 it had condemned monoenergism and monothelitism as heresies.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monothelitism">Monothelitism</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">921 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,105 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles the Simple and Henry the Fowler sign the Treaty of Bonn</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-simple">Charles the Simple</a>, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-francia">West Francia</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-fowler">Henry the Fowler</a>, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-francia">East Francia</a>, signed a &quot;pact of friendship&quot; aboard a ship in the middle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bonn">Bonn</a>. The river was the border between their kingdoms.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-simple">Charles the Simple</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-fowler">Henry the Fowler</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hanoi" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hanoi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1426 CE <span class="tih-ago">600 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lam Sơn rebels ambush and rout a Ming army near Hanoi</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Armed with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hand-cannon">hand cannons</a>, Vietnamese rebels under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/le-loi">Lê Lợi</a> ambushed and routed a Ming army under General Wang Tong between the villages of Tốt Động and Chúc Động, near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanoi">Hanoi</a>. It was the decisive battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lam-son-uprising">Lam Sơn uprising</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lam-son-uprising">Lam Sơn uprising</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ming-empire">Ming Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1492">1492 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">534 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Ensisheim meteorite falls in Alsace</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A stony meteorite fell in a wheat field outside the walled town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ensisheim">Ensisheim</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a>. It is the oldest recorded meteorite fall in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> whose stone survives, and it can still be seen in the town's museum.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ensisheim">Ensisheim</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1665">1665 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">361 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Oxford Gazette, later the London Gazette, is first published</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With the court in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxford">Oxford</a> to escape the plague, the first issue of the Oxford Gazette appeared. Renamed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> Gazette, it is the oldest continuously published newspaper in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxford">Oxford</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1837">1837 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">189 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A pro-slavery mob kills Elijah Lovejoy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The abolitionist editor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elijah">Elijah</a> Lovejoy was shot defending his fourth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> press from a mob in Alton, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illinois">Illinois</a>. His death turned many northerners towards the anti-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a> cause.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1867">1867 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">159 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Marie Curie is born in Warsaw</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Maria Skłodowska was born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a>, then under Russian rule. As Marie Curie she pioneered research on radioactivity and became the first person to win <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-prize">Nobel Prizes</a> in two sciences.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1917">1917 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">109 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Bolsheviks seize power in Petrograd</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Bolshevik-led Red Guards took key points in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a> and stormed the Winter Palace overnight, toppling the Provisional Government. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/october-revolution">October Revolution</a>, so called from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julian-calendar">Julian calendar</a>, led to the Soviet state.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julian-calendar">Julian calendar</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1940">1940 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Tacoma Narrows Bridge collapses</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Four months after opening, the suspension bridge over Puget Sound twisted violently in a 40-mile-per-hour wind and fell into the water. Filmed footage of 'Galloping Gertie' transformed bridge aerodynamics.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 7 November <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/constans-ii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/constans-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Constans II</span><span class="tp">630–668</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francisco-de-zurbaran"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francisco-de-zurbaran.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Francisco de Zurbarán</span><span class="tp">1598–1664</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/james-cook"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/james-cook.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">James Cook</span><span class="tp">1728–1779</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/nestor-makhno"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/nestor-makhno.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Nestor Makhno</span><span class="tp">1888–1934</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/albert-camus"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/albert-camus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Albert Camus</span><span class="tp">1913–1960</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
